  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USAID Media-Kyrgyzstan, Media-K, Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Kyrgyz Republic):  USAID&apos;s Media Activity will continue to strengthen Kyrgyz citizens&apos; awareness, engagement and participation in the social, economic and political processes by increasing the viability, professionalism and vibrancy of local, factual, and diverse independent media in the Kyrgyz Republic.  It will partner with local media outlets and organizations to achieve this goal through four interdependent objectives: 1) increase entrepreneurial and innovative content offerings through training and content grants; 2) Localize media development efforts and, grow local technical expertise for media practitioners through training, mentorship, and organizational development; 3) improve local market conditions for local media and local media management practice by expanding market information and business consulting for local outlets; and, 4) strengthen local resilience to disinformation by supporting existing Kyrgyz efforts to counter disinformation and increase media literacy. The activity will emphasize support for media outlets outside of Bishkek, developing these small media enterprises, and increasing production of more engaging and data driven local content in the Kyrgyz language. This activity will support ICS objective 3.3: An inclusive democracy featuring promotion of human rights and vibrant, effective civic engagement. USAID&apos;s contributions to meeting the $12,000,000 DRG and $2,300,000 Microenterprise directives through this IM are $1,500,000 and $300,000 respectively.</narrative>
  </description>
